        statement: n = 2k + 1 for an integer k.
        justification: Use the parity definition.
      - id: proof-ArrangeSteps-Contrapositive-v4-2
        statement: "3n\xB2 = 12k\xB2 + 12k + 3."
        justification: Substitute and simplify.
      - id: proof-ArrangeSteps-Contrapositive-v4-3
        statement: "3n\xB2 = 2(6k\xB2 + 6k + 1) + 1, which is odd."
        justification: Identify the opposite parity.
      - id: proof-ArrangeSteps-Contrapositive-v4-4
        statement: "Therefore 3n\xB2 even implies n even."
        justification: Conclude by contrapositive.
